# Phase 19 basic Docker Broker profile — 2026-10-17T04:33:17Z

- Image: official `apache/rocketmq:5.3.4`, pinned to multi-platform index
  `sha256:d57ee4ebbd9d7bb6e185775bde41c128e98f185b25bf0b05c77d4e6c010572b8`.
  The selected linux/arm64 image digest is
  `sha256:4c7982d63c1b1d0edb45d6e9d330746b0a7816d96d01daa340244f5fad84d215`;
  the image reports RocketMQ 5.3.4 and OpenJDK 8u472.
- Docker Engine 29.8.2 and Docker Compose v5.5.0 are available. The basic
  profile uses a project-scoped network and store volume, binds host ports to
  loopback, disables automatic topic/subscription-group creation, and advertises
  the Broker as `broker:10911` for clients on the Compose network.
- Provisioning used the required disposable marker and explicit `basic` profile:
  `ROCKETMQ_CLASSIC_TEST_ENV=local-disposable ROCKETMQ_PROFILE=basic` with
  project `rocketmq-classic-p19-20261017-0429`.
- The first startup failed closed because an empty Docker named volume was
  root-owned and the image's `rocketmq` user could not create its store lock.
  Added a one-shot `store-init` service that sets the project volume owner to
  the image's `rocketmq` user. The rerun passed `docker compose up --wait` and
  bounded `mqadmin clusterList` polling. Both services became healthy and the
  cluster listing reported `RocketMQLocalTest`, `broker-a`, address
  `broker:10911`, and version `V5_3_4`.
- Archived container startup logs in
  [`17-phase-19-basic-broker-profile__20261017T043317Z.log`](17-phase-19-basic-broker-profile__20261017T043317Z.log).
  `cleanup.sh` stopped and removed only this Compose project, its network, and
  its store volume; subsequent project-filtered container and volume listings
  were empty.
- This verifies the initial environment setup/readiness slice only. No
  Java/Rust client scenario ran; no topic/group scenario state was created.
  The fail-closed scenario runner, per-scenario reset/evidence reconciliation,
  two-Broker, TLS/auth and other required profiles, and the complete local
  matrix remain open. This work stays automatic Phase 19 work and is not moved
  to the owner-manual validation list.
